[{:db/id "q-82397/selection/16b50194516e7dcad35bdecafc4c70a67642e9c995267daaf0accfcc873be095" :answer/id #uuid "b1142ecb-cea7-5d54-be7b-a6b80307ec31" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82397/selection/ada5cc9b7cb3c1f0ee40e3f0daf3ce48624840426207eb57c599d2352c73fca0" :answer/id #uuid "0a1df854-3999-56fa-98f9-ffcea6dccd34" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U$ and $V$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82397/selection/04646d488959d0b10c98bd9055615c2535925a7b59f21ec7dcdb79a9fb18da0d" :answer/id #uuid "8e027f2e-e9a0-5b8f-a460-f3fe05113e93" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U$ and $W$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82397/selection/6c5d8db382b33f30f332b189fe1fe2973356c5fdb6f69748c83cf4a47a8bf0ab" :answer/id #uuid "53c0b04a-8658-5a50-a3da-abf81c739694" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$V$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82397/selection/1454d2f1915a335c7d01677c9b98fbae5aedebb848a7a30361c0ea47ca70fb1e" :answer/id #uuid "20f38fcf-9181-515f-abae-cf3d74922a49" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$V$ and $W$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82397/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "23a1f73f-be8b-5c97-9656-af3031f13b76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-82397/selection/ada5cc9b7cb3c1f0ee40e3f0daf3ce48624840426207eb57c599d2352c73fca0" :answer-field/choices ["q-82397/selection/16b50194516e7dcad35bdecafc4c70a67642e9c995267daaf0accfcc873be095" "q-82397/selection/ada5cc9b7cb3c1f0ee40e3f0daf3ce48624840426207eb57c599d2352c73fca0" "q-82397/selection/04646d488959d0b10c98bd9055615c2535925a7b59f21ec7dcdb79a9fb18da0d" "q-82397/selection/6c5d8db382b33f30f332b189fe1fe2973356c5fdb6f69748c83cf4a47a8bf0ab" "q-82397/selection/1454d2f1915a335c7d01677c9b98fbae5aedebb848a7a30361c0ea47ca70fb1e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-82397" :question/id #uuid "791094d3-0869-53a1-bd62-582e012d4cec" :question/math-academy-id "q-82397" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthogonal?\n\n- $U={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $V={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $W={[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n${{u}_{1},{u}_{2},{u}_{3}},$ \n${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}},$ and \n${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthogonal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,\\,{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0,\\,{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0.$\n\n- ${v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0.$\n\n- ${w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-1+3-1-1=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=1+0-2+1=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=-1+0+2-1=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $U$ is orthogonal.\n\n- For the set $V,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=2-1-1=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $V$ is orthogonal.\n\n- For the set $W,$ notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]=-15+24=9\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $W$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$U$ and $V$ only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-82397/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee1838df-f1d6-5bc4-908c-b96e2ad577c9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82397"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83719/selection/04646d488959d0b10c98bd9055615c2535925a7b59f21ec7dcdb79a9fb18da0d" :answer/id #uuid "9f9d50ab-0418-578c-a616-2a9c87b4b5a9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U$ and $W$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83719/selection/ada5cc9b7cb3c1f0ee40e3f0daf3ce48624840426207eb57c599d2352c73fca0" :answer/id #uuid "90d299d0-091f-562a-b944-63c65d0705a9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U$ and $V$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83719/selection/16b50194516e7dcad35bdecafc4c70a67642e9c995267daaf0accfcc873be095" :answer/id #uuid "1e018e13-e8d9-5fdf-96af-f0ee2aa3be01" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83719/selection/e2d52a456cba49e8b5bad42a80eb2a8b1b2bb244f8c178b51f34d013592f152f" :answer/id #uuid "1463e04b-8a4c-50d1-88de-13e82c028330" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$W$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83719/selection/1454d2f1915a335c7d01677c9b98fbae5aedebb848a7a30361c0ea47ca70fb1e" :answer/id #uuid "83f47a32-f1cb-57f1-b36a-a6fe84230d31" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$V$ and $W$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83719/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dcdf2b2e-4f90-5cfb-8d15-39df6c5db160" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83719/selection/04646d488959d0b10c98bd9055615c2535925a7b59f21ec7dcdb79a9fb18da0d" :answer-field/choices ["q-83719/selection/04646d488959d0b10c98bd9055615c2535925a7b59f21ec7dcdb79a9fb18da0d" "q-83719/selection/ada5cc9b7cb3c1f0ee40e3f0daf3ce48624840426207eb57c599d2352c73fca0" "q-83719/selection/16b50194516e7dcad35bdecafc4c70a67642e9c995267daaf0accfcc873be095" "q-83719/selection/e2d52a456cba49e8b5bad42a80eb2a8b1b2bb244f8c178b51f34d013592f152f" "q-83719/selection/1454d2f1915a335c7d01677c9b98fbae5aedebb848a7a30361c0ea47ca70fb1e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83719" :question/id #uuid "9a49bdd8-1b47-5f19-a5c1-f6bf1e352872" :question/math-academy-id "q-83719" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthogonal?\n\n- $U={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $V={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $W={[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n${{u}_{1},{u}_{2},{u}_{3}},$ \n${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}},$ and \n${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthogonal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,\\,{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0,\\,{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0.$\n\n- ${v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0,\\,{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,\\,{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{3}=0.$\n\n- ${w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=-1+0+1=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0+0+0=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0+0+0=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $U$ is orthogonal.\n\n- For the set $V,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=12+0+1=13\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]=-40+40=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $W$ is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$U$ and $W$ only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83719/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee1838df-f1d6-5bc4-908c-b96e2ad577c9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83719"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-82396/selection/04646d488959d0b10c98bd9055615c2535925a7b59f21ec7dcdb79a9fb18da0d" :answer/id #uuid "d6ebabd9-2247-5907-afd6-10e1f2ee0f47" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U$ and $W$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82396/selection/1454d2f1915a335c7d01677c9b98fbae5aedebb848a7a30361c0ea47ca70fb1e" :answer/id #uuid "06bb32a6-20a4-58fd-9811-86956aa30ba0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$V$ and $W$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82396/selection/16b50194516e7dcad35bdecafc4c70a67642e9c995267daaf0accfcc873be095" :answer/id #uuid "2db4a1c7-3132-5e39-9b02-5fa0ac42988c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82396/selection/e2d52a456cba49e8b5bad42a80eb2a8b1b2bb244f8c178b51f34d013592f152f" :answer/id #uuid "34597237-688d-528c-95ba-10b85c18591a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$W$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82396/selection/6c5d8db382b33f30f332b189fe1fe2973356c5fdb6f69748c83cf4a47a8bf0ab" :a