rn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-10-3+0=-13\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $U$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\n- For the set $V,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=-18-2=-20\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=2-1-1=0 & ✓ \\\\ {w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=0-1+1=0 & ✓ \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=0+1-1=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $W$ is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$W$ only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-82396/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee1838df-f1d6-5bc4-908c-b96e2ad577c9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82396"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140480/selection/e2d52a456cba49e8b5bad42a80eb2a8b1b2bb244f8c178b51f34d013592f152f" :answer/id #uuid "52b11d19-9fea-518c-9cc9-6c98fc1c6506" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$W$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140480/selection/04646d488959d0b10c98bd9055615c2535925a7b59f21ec7dcdb79a9fb18da0d" :answer/id #uuid "9406119e-4d2c-575e-9aad-b75e4f52a5e8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U$ and $W$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140480/selection/16b50194516e7dcad35bdecafc4c70a67642e9c995267daaf0accfcc873be095" :answer/id #uuid "ef4327fc-8a74-5938-b491-e81494ed6fe9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140480/selection/ab8d6b18df33f8e8fa60e39210be9f712081961173da5def9d5ce08c80d2fd6d" :answer/id #uuid "1ef3c437-7fd1-5007-b849-89afa1b00f44" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U,$ $V$ and $W$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140480/selection/ada5cc9b7cb3c1f0ee40e3f0daf3ce48624840426207eb57c599d2352c73fca0" :answer/id #uuid "8f2b4924-7608-53a2-a2ed-b08fb8d34cd0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U$ and $V$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140480/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "378bf095-ea7e-53a1-a97a-9ecf89cc0c00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140480/selection/04646d488959d0b10c98bd9055615c2535925a7b59f21ec7dcdb79a9fb18da0d" :answer-field/choices ["q-140480/selection/e2d52a456cba49e8b5bad42a80eb2a8b1b2bb244f8c178b51f34d013592f152f" "q-140480/selection/04646d488959d0b10c98bd9055615c2535925a7b59f21ec7dcdb79a9fb18da0d" "q-140480/selection/16b50194516e7dcad35bdecafc4c70a67642e9c995267daaf0accfcc873be095" "q-140480/selection/ab8d6b18df33f8e8fa60e39210be9f712081961173da5def9d5ce08c80d2fd6d" "q-140480/selection/ada5cc9b7cb3c1f0ee40e3f0daf3ce48624840426207eb57c599d2352c73fca0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140480" :question/id #uuid "adea282e-6aaa-5784-aa8d-026ea45a32cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-140480" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthogonal?\n\n- $U={[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $V={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $W={[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n${{u}_{1},{u}_{2}},$ \n${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}},$ and \n${{w}_{1},{w}_{2},{w}_{3}},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthogonal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0.$\n\n- ${v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0.$\n\n- ${w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0,\\,{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{3}=0,\\,{w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{3}=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=10-9-1=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $U$ is orthogonal.\n\n- For the set $V,$ notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=4-4+4=4\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=10-9-1=0 & ✓ \\\\ {w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]=0+3-3=0 & ✓ \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]=0-3+3=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $W$ is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$U$ and $W$ only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140480/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee1838df-f1d6-5bc4-908c-b96e2ad577c9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140480"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-39396/selection/6c5d8db382b33f30f332b189fe1fe2973356c5fdb6f69748c83cf4a47a8bf0ab" :answer/id #uuid "00763332-aeb9-50fc-8e1f-7deefc8c45f0" :answer/type :answer.ty